1
00:00:01,001 --> 00:00:03,336
[theme music playing]

2
00:00:03,420 --> 00:00:06,464
[tense music playing]

3
00:00:20,353 --> 00:00:21,604
[screaming]

4
00:00:21,688 --> 00:00:23,773
[shattering sound]

5
00:00:27,402 --> 00:00:28,528
HAPPY CENTENNIAL,
POBLACION ARDIENTE!

6
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:32,240
[host] <i>Let's all give</i>
<i>a warm round of applause</i>

7
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:35,452
-<i>for the Ardiente family!</i>
-[applause]

8
00:00:35,535 --> 00:00:37,746
[man] <i>Ma'am, someone asked me</i>
<i>to give this to you.</i>

9
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,874
[Emilia] <i>This is impossible.</i>
<i>This is not happening.</i>

10
00:00:40,957 --> 00:00:42,041
<i>You're dead.</i>

11
00:00:42,125 --> 00:00:46,796
[Lily] <i>You're right, Emilia.</i>
<i>Ivy Aguas is dead.</i>

12
00:00:47,213 --> 00:00:51,843
[Julio] <i>If anyone dares to take</i>
<i>this province for themselves,</i>

13
00:00:51,926 --> 00:00:54,763
<i>they will answer to me.</i>

14
00:00:54,846 --> 00:01:00,477
<i>Because the truth will always,</i>
<i>without a doubt, prevail!</i>

15
00:01:00,560 --> 00:01:02,145
<i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

16
00:01:02,228 --> 00:01:04,564
[in unison] <i>Viva Ardiente!</i>

17
00:01:06,691 --> 00:01:10,612
[Lily] <i>This is justice</i>
<i>for Poblacion Ardiente!</i>

18
00:01:11,112 --> 00:01:14,365
<i>No matter how high</i>
<i>you've exalted yourself,</i>

19
00:01:14,449 --> 00:01:15,867
<i>I, Lily Cruz,</i>

20
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:19,245
<i>will drag you down</i>
<i>to where you truly belong!</i>

21
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:20,955
-[Raul] <i>Arnaldo!</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Arnaldo!</i>

22
00:01:21,414 --> 00:01:24,584
[Camia] <i>I never thought</i>
<i>this day would come.</i>

23
00:01:24,667 --> 00:01:26,085
[Lily, crying] <i>This is my victory.</i>

24
00:01:26,169 --> 00:01:27,670
<i>To finally be with you.</i>

25
00:01:27,754 --> 00:01:31,508
<i>The two of us together,</i>
<i>along with everyone I love.</i>

26
00:01:31,591 --> 00:01:33,176
[Emilia] <i>You can post your bail,</i>

27
00:01:33,259 --> 00:01:35,428
<i>but you can't return</i>
<i>to being a governor again.</i>

28
00:01:35,512 --> 00:01:38,473
<i>Papa, you're so doomed. You are so doomed.</i>

29
00:01:40,099 --> 00:01:42,685
[soft piano music playing]

30
00:01:54,531 --> 00:01:55,490
Lily.

31
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,700
Why did you bring those things out again?

32
00:02:03,498 --> 00:02:05,125
I just really missed Dad again.

33
00:02:06,626 --> 00:02:09,629
The Ardientes may have gotten
what they deserved, but…

34
00:02:13,550 --> 00:02:19,013
it would've been better
if Dad were still with us today.

35
00:02:21,349 --> 00:02:24,936
I remember all the things he did for me.

36
00:02:28,022 --> 00:02:30,483
This was our favorite book, remember?

37
00:02:31,901 --> 00:02:32,944
Every night,

38
00:02:35,238 --> 00:02:36,948
he would read this to me.

39
00:02:38,825 --> 00:02:40,660
Ever since then…

40
00:02:45,707 --> 00:02:47,584
he's been an inspiration to me.

41
00:02:54,883 --> 00:02:55,967
Lily…

42
00:02:57,635 --> 00:03:02,682
I'm sure your father's
smiling down on you from above

43
00:03:04,851 --> 00:03:07,020
because you've grown into such a brave

44
00:03:07,770 --> 00:03:09,188
and determined woman

45
00:03:10,732 --> 00:03:12,734
with a good heart.

46
00:03:13,610 --> 00:03:18,031
[sentimental music playing]

47
00:03:36,883 --> 00:03:40,470
I did not hire you to give me excuses!

48
00:03:40,553 --> 00:03:42,096
Just go do your job!

49
00:03:43,765 --> 00:03:45,391
Papa, calm down.

50
00:03:45,475 --> 00:03:48,561
Why are you so stressed when you
just got out of the hospital?

51
00:03:48,645 --> 00:03:50,480
-What if you get a heart attack?
-[slams table]

52
00:03:50,563 --> 00:03:53,149
It's all that Lily Cruz's fault!

53
00:03:54,567 --> 00:03:58,404
Oh, Papa. I've been telling you for ages

54
00:03:58,488 --> 00:04:02,325
that Ivy Aguas and Lily Cruz
are the same person,

55
00:04:02,408 --> 00:04:04,077
but you wouldn't listen.

56
00:04:04,160 --> 00:04:07,997
This is just another case
of "I told you so."

57
00:04:08,081 --> 00:04:12,794
Emilia, you're worried
I'll have a heart attack, right?

58
00:04:13,211 --> 00:04:16,547
So, why does it seem like
you're making me even angrier?

59
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:20,760
And besides, who do you think

60
00:04:20,843 --> 00:04:23,805
is responsible for incurring
that woman's wrath?

61
00:04:23,888 --> 00:04:25,056
Isn't it you?!

62
00:04:25,306 --> 00:04:26,557
-No!
-[Julio scoffs]

63
00:04:26,975 --> 00:04:29,978
You're the one who had
Lily Cruz's father killed,

64
00:04:30,937 --> 00:04:33,273
and later on, had her mother raped.

65
00:04:33,690 --> 00:04:36,234
Then, you insisted
on killing Lily Cruz herself!

66
00:04:36,317 --> 00:04:38,695
But, lo and behold, what happened?!

67
00:04:38,945 --> 00:04:42,240
Now, she's alive and out for revenge!

68
00:04:42,323 --> 00:04:43,283
[inhales deeply]

69
00:04:43,366 --> 00:04:44,826
Therefore, you should be blamed

70
00:04:44,909 --> 00:04:47,829
for whatever misfortune
befalls this family.

71
00:04:47,912 --> 00:04:50,707
[gloomy music playing]

72
00:04:51,291 --> 00:04:52,417
[exhales sharply]

73
00:04:53,042 --> 00:04:54,585
[knocks on door] Papa?

74
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,380
Papa, I heard you shouting
from outside. Shouldn't you be--

75
00:04:57,463 --> 00:04:59,841
Oh, shut up! You're another one to blame!

76
00:04:59,924 --> 00:05:02,593
You are at the very heart of this mess!

77
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,096
The both of you.

78
00:05:05,179 --> 00:05:06,222
[Emilia clears throat]

79
00:05:06,306 --> 00:05:08,808
You attempted to kill Lily Cruz's family

80
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,935
many moons ago, but you failed!

81
00:05:11,519 --> 00:05:12,895
Do you really want me

82
00:05:12,979 --> 00:05:15,523
to teach you the proper way
of disposing of troublemakers?

83
00:05:16,482 --> 00:05:19,068
Papa, with all due respect, but…

84
00:05:19,736 --> 00:05:21,446
don't you think someone
looking for revenge

85
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:23,406
was bound to happen? I think so.

86
00:05:24,699 --> 00:05:26,701
Excuse me?!

87
00:05:26,951 --> 00:05:28,786
Well, you know…

88
00:05:29,287 --> 00:05:31,998
Let's face it. To be frank, Papa,

89
00:05:32,081 --> 00:05:34,917
this family has ruined
so many people's lives,

90
00:05:35,001 --> 00:05:36,127
not just Lily Cruz's.

91
00:05:36,210 --> 00:05:38,671
There are tons of people
who'd want to make you pay.

92
00:05:38,755 --> 00:05:40,631
So, if you ask me, I really think

93
00:05:40,715 --> 00:05:45,887
we should just calm down
and stop fighting each other.

94
00:05:45,970 --> 00:05:48,389
Or else, we'll only cause
this family's downfall.

95
00:05:49,098 --> 00:05:50,349
[clapping] Wow!

96
00:05:52,226 --> 00:05:58,608
Since when did your little black
heart develop a conscience?

97
00:05:59,734 --> 00:06:01,694
Well, let me remind you.

98
00:06:02,945 --> 00:06:06,949
Weren't you the one
who kept Camia Cruz alive?!

99
00:06:08,326 --> 00:06:14,123
And yet, you get to go away unscathed!

100
00:06:15,541 --> 00:06:16,501
-Huh?!
-Papa.

101
00:06:16,584 --> 00:06:17,460
-No!
-Papa!

102
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:19,420
-Papa, no!
-Calm down.

103
00:06:20,213 --> 00:06:23,424
-You know what? Just get out.
-[suspenseful music playing]

104
00:06:24,175 --> 00:06:25,384
Just get out.

105
00:06:25,468 --> 00:06:26,552
[Raul mumbles]

106
00:06:27,553 --> 00:06:30,014
Both of you. I said get out.

107
00:06:32,391 --> 00:06:33,434
[exhales sharply]

108
00:06:33,518 --> 00:06:34,769
[breathing heavily]

109
00:06:34,852 --> 00:06:35,812
[groans]

110
00:06:41,526 --> 00:06:44,862
I will never forget the name "Ivy Aguas."

111
00:06:45,655 --> 00:06:47,198
After all,

112
00:06:48,366 --> 00:06:51,285
she's the one who fought all the pain

113
00:06:51,369 --> 00:06:52,453
that Lily went through.

114
00:06:52,537 --> 00:06:54,705
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

115
00:06:55,790 --> 00:06:58,459
Well, not all of Lily's memories were bad.

116
00:07:00,044 --> 00:07:03,965
She's had some good ones too. Right?

117
00:07:10,721 --> 00:07:12,014
But for now,

118
00:07:13,141 --> 00:07:15,226
you need to let Ivy Aguas go.

119
00:07:16,102 --> 00:07:19,439
Be Lily again. Embrace your true identity.

120
00:07:23,776 --> 00:07:25,069
You're right, Jepoy.

121
00:07:26,446 --> 00:07:28,781
Ivy Aguas' mission has come to an end.

122
00:07:29,407 --> 00:07:31,242
"Ivy Aguas" was just a name.

123
00:07:32,118 --> 00:07:35,455
That strength and courage to
fight against the Ardientes…

124
00:07:37,165 --> 00:07:38,875
I know that was all Lily Cruz.

125
00:07:40,418 --> 00:07:43,713
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

126
00:08:01,397 --> 00:08:02,565
[Diego flicks lighter]

127
00:08:05,943 --> 00:08:09,447
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

128
00:08:19,123 --> 00:08:20,208
Dad.

129
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:25,880
Dad, thank you

130
00:08:26,422 --> 00:08:28,174
<i>for guiding me.</i>

131
00:08:31,135 --> 00:08:33,221
<i>Even now,</i>

132
00:08:35,264 --> 00:08:36,974
<i>all those lessons you taught me…</i>

133
00:08:38,976 --> 00:08:40,394
<i>I still keep them close.</i>

134
00:08:43,105 --> 00:08:48,110
<i>You taught me how to value life</i>

135
00:08:49,362 --> 00:08:50,571
<i>and morality.</i>

136
00:08:53,199 --> 00:08:54,909
I wish you were here, Dad.

137
00:08:56,827 --> 00:08:57,912
I wish…

138
00:09:01,332 --> 00:09:02,625
you were still here.

139
00:09:12,969 --> 00:09:14,345
I love you, Dad.

140
00:09:16,264 --> 00:09:17,515
I love you.

141
00:09:20,560 --> 00:09:23,813
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

142
00:09:39,287 --> 00:09:40,538
Nanny Carlotta,

143
00:09:42,707 --> 00:09:44,041
I miss you so much.

144
00:09:46,043 --> 00:09:47,044
Nanny…

145
00:09:48,671 --> 00:09:50,965
I finally got the upper hand
against the Ardientes.

146
00:09:52,967 --> 00:09:56,262
And if you were here,
I know you'd tell me…

147
00:10:00,182 --> 00:10:02,101
how happy you are for me.

148
00:10:03,352 --> 00:10:04,353
Nanny…

149
00:10:06,564 --> 00:10:07,607
Thank you.

150
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:12,528
<i>Thank you for loving me,</i>

151
00:10:15,323 --> 00:10:17,408
<i>and for taking care of me.</i>

152
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:21,746
<i>It made me stronger each time.</i>

153
00:10:23,956 --> 00:10:25,041
[Lily sniffles]

154
00:10:25,583 --> 00:10:27,543
<i>I love you so much, Nanny.</i>

155
00:10:33,716 --> 00:10:34,592
[sniffles]

156
00:10:34,675 --> 00:10:36,344
I'm sorry I wasn't there.

157
00:10:45,019 --> 00:10:46,354
I love you.

158
00:10:48,814 --> 00:10:52,735
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

159
00:11:07,375 --> 00:11:08,417
[Lily] Ms. Prianka…

160
00:11:10,336 --> 00:11:13,631
You gave me a second chance at life.

161
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:21,180
You taught me…

162
00:11:24,183 --> 00:11:28,270
<i>how hard you should strive</i>
<i>for what you want.</i>

163
00:11:32,274 --> 00:11:34,652
<i>You even taught me how to run a business.</i>

164
00:11:35,903 --> 00:11:37,696
<i>You taught me</i>

165
00:11:39,156 --> 00:11:40,616
<i>how to be strong.</i>

166
00:11:41,992 --> 00:11:43,119
<i>To be strong</i>

167
00:11:44,412 --> 00:11:46,455
so that I could find justice.

168
00:11:48,499 --> 00:11:50,292
Ms. Prianka, I know…

169
00:11:54,880 --> 00:11:56,715
how you were always there

170
00:11:58,509 --> 00:11:59,718
for all my battles.

171
00:12:04,181 --> 00:12:06,142
I know you're always with me.

172
00:12:12,189 --> 00:12:13,315
Thank you…

173
00:12:16,986 --> 00:12:22,241
for taking me in
and treating me like your own.

174
00:12:24,702 --> 00:12:27,329
You gave me your name.

175
00:12:28,372 --> 00:12:29,248
[sniffles]

176
00:12:29,331 --> 00:12:32,501
You named me "Ivy Aguas."

177
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:38,507
You taught me how to fight back.

178
00:12:41,385 --> 00:12:45,264
And I'll never forget
everything you taught me.

179
00:12:46,307 --> 00:12:47,308
[sniffles]

180
00:12:47,391 --> 00:12:54,356
I'll never ever forget all the efforts
you made to teach me.

181
00:12:57,318 --> 00:12:59,111
I love you, Ms. Prianka.

182
00:13:04,783 --> 00:13:06,619
Thank you so much.

183
00:13:06,702 --> 00:13:08,954
["Wildflower" instrumental playing]

184
00:13:20,216 --> 00:13:23,219
[whispering] Thank you. For everything.

185
00:13:29,934 --> 00:13:31,268
Hi. Good morning, Papa.

186
00:13:31,352 --> 00:13:32,603
Good morning.

187
00:13:33,687 --> 00:13:34,688
[groans]

188
00:13:36,815 --> 00:13:42,947
Wow! I can smell breakfast
from my bedroom.

189
00:13:43,030 --> 00:13:44,740
This is nice.

190
00:13:45,950 --> 00:13:48,035
I'm so hungry, I could eat a horse.

191
00:13:48,827 --> 00:13:50,996
-Okay.
-Oops. Papa, wait.

192
00:13:51,080 --> 00:13:54,208
This is not your breakfast.
Hold on. Jenny!

193
00:13:54,291 --> 00:13:55,417
-What?
-Jenny!

194
00:13:55,501 --> 00:13:57,336
What do you mean this is not my breakfast?

195
00:13:57,419 --> 00:14:00,798
Yes. We prepared a special
breakfast for you, Papa.

196
00:14:04,218 --> 00:14:05,261
There.

197
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:11,100
What is this?! You expect me to eat this?

198
00:14:11,183 --> 00:14:13,978
This is what makes people sick.

199
00:14:14,061 --> 00:14:15,980
Papa, stop complaining.

200
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:18,190
You have to live healthy.

201
00:14:18,274 --> 00:14:21,694
Remember? And eating
healthy food will help you.

202
00:14:21,777 --> 00:14:24,697
I don't want you to die. When you do,

203
00:14:24,780 --> 00:14:27,825
you'll be forgotten.
It's not your time yet.

204
00:14:27,908 --> 00:14:29,118
[Julio] Stop it!

205
00:14:29,493 --> 00:14:30,953
[Emilia] Eat, Papa. Come on. Fruits.

206
00:14:31,537 --> 00:14:34,039
[Julio] What?! What's this?! What the--

207
00:14:34,123 --> 00:14:36,166
-Papa.
-What right does this--

208
00:14:36,250 --> 00:14:37,960
That's enough. There you go again.

209
00:14:38,043 --> 00:14:39,879
Be easy on your heart.

210
00:14:39,962 --> 00:14:42,548
Stop it. I know you want
me healthy, but stop it!

211
00:14:43,048 --> 00:14:44,758
You don't have to be rubbing it in.

212
00:14:44,842 --> 00:14:45,885
[newspaper thuds]

213
00:14:45,968 --> 00:14:48,345
-You're so grumpy today.
-[Julio groans]

214
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:50,139
Oh, the attorney's here.

215
00:14:50,472 --> 00:14:52,308
-Attorney, good morning.
-Good morning, Governor.

216
00:14:52,391 --> 00:14:54,393
Please, please give me some good news.

217
00:14:54,476 --> 00:14:56,312
Make my day, please.

218
00:14:56,395 --> 00:14:57,897
You'll want to hear this, Governor.

219
00:14:58,606 --> 00:15:00,941
Their opposition
to your bail posting got denied.

220
00:15:01,025 --> 00:15:02,192
[gasps]

221
00:15:02,484 --> 00:15:05,487
So, it means I remain free, right?

222
00:15:05,738 --> 00:15:08,073
-Yes.
-[Julio laughing maniacally]

223
00:15:09,658 --> 00:15:10,910
I knew it!

224
00:15:12,202 --> 00:15:14,121
I am Julio Ardiente,

225
00:15:14,496 --> 00:15:20,085
and I always get what I want
no matter how big or small.

226
00:15:20,169 --> 00:15:21,712
-And this is mine.
-Papa!

227
00:15:21,795 --> 00:15:23,213
You're not supposed to eat that.

228
00:15:23,631 --> 00:15:24,548
[taunting]

229
00:15:24,632 --> 00:15:25,883
[muffled laugh]

230
00:15:26,467 --> 00:15:27,843
Unbelievable.

231
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:29,470
[moans]

232
00:15:30,930 --> 00:15:32,681
[Emilia] Join us, Attorney, for breakfast.

233
00:15:33,891 --> 00:15:34,642
[security guard] Careful.

234
00:15:34,725 --> 00:15:37,102
Take that directly to the storage room.

235
00:15:38,228 --> 00:15:39,229
-Hurry up.
-Hey!

236
00:15:40,105 --> 00:15:41,148
What are you doing?

237
00:15:41,231 --> 00:15:43,525
[security guard] Excuse me, sir.
You're not allowed here.

238
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:51,951
Are you out of your mind, boy?
Do you know who I am?

239
00:15:52,868 --> 00:15:57,164
I am Governor Julio Ardiente.

240
00:15:57,247 --> 00:15:58,916
[tense music playing]

241
00:15:58,999 --> 00:16:00,334
-I'll handle this.
-Yes, sir.

242
00:16:01,335 --> 00:16:03,003
-Disrespectful--
-Julio.

243
00:16:04,296 --> 00:16:05,965
Last time I checked,

244
00:16:06,340 --> 00:16:09,259
you had a problem
with your heart, not your head.

245
00:16:09,343 --> 00:16:12,304
So, why is it so hard for you
to understand the law?

246
00:16:12,888 --> 00:16:15,099
Or… Or is it just old age?

247
00:16:15,808 --> 00:16:20,938
Stop playing house in my territory.

248
00:16:21,021 --> 00:16:23,065
I'm not playing house.

249
00:16:23,941 --> 00:16:26,485
This is the house
of the governor and that's me.

250
00:16:26,944 --> 00:16:28,779
I am the governor.

251
00:16:28,862 --> 00:16:30,739
[laughing]

252
00:16:31,365 --> 00:16:33,367
[tense music playing]

253
00:16:33,450 --> 00:16:34,284
[Julio sighs]

254
00:16:34,368 --> 00:16:37,162
Here's a letter from the
Office of the Ombudsman.

255
00:16:38,789 --> 00:16:40,958
[tense music playing]

256
00:16:45,170 --> 00:16:48,424
[Julio] "90-day suspension."

257
00:16:48,966 --> 00:16:51,051
What am I? A student?

258
00:16:52,594 --> 00:17:00,144
I won't let a stupid letter
tell me what to do.

259
00:17:00,978 --> 00:17:03,480
You do know what you're doing
is illegal, right?

260
00:17:03,981 --> 00:17:07,985
So, if I were you,
I'd avoid trouble and leave.

261
00:17:08,694 --> 00:17:12,489
You know, even if I were
to build an office

262
00:17:12,948 --> 00:17:15,075
at the entrance of this capitol,

263
00:17:16,035 --> 00:17:17,661
there's nothing you could do about it.

264
00:17:17,745 --> 00:17:22,249
No one can stop me. No one.

265
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,460
Suit yourself.

266
00:17:25,377 --> 00:17:28,464
[tense music playing]

267
00:17:34,970 --> 00:17:39,224
[crowd chanting] <i>Governor Julio!</i>
<i>Governor Julio! Governor Julio!</i>

268
00:17:45,230 --> 00:17:48,442
[Lily] <i>No matter how high</i>
<i>you've exalted yourself,</i>

269
00:17:49,193 --> 00:17:54,156
<i>I, Lily Cruz, will drag you down</i>
<i>to where you truly belong!</i>

270
00:17:54,740 --> 00:18:00,079
[Julio] <i>You can't do this to me!</i>
<i>I am Julio Ardiente!</i>

271
00:18:01,080 --> 00:18:03,749
[tense music playing]

272
00:18:14,259 --> 00:18:15,385
[music stops]

273
00:18:15,469 --> 00:18:17,638
Raul is just so reckless.

274
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:20,933
How can he possibly believe
that Papa will change?

275
00:18:21,016 --> 00:18:23,602
Seriously? Does he think
this is a fairy tale

276
00:18:23,685 --> 00:18:26,563
where the evil villains
learn their lesson at the end?

277
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:27,731
No way!

278
00:18:28,816 --> 00:18:30,109
[in distorted voice]
If that's the case, Emilia,

279
00:18:30,526 --> 00:18:32,861
why did you defend him from Julio?

280
00:18:33,445 --> 00:18:37,074
You should've just let him die.

281
00:18:38,158 --> 00:18:40,869
Because I don't want any more commotion.

282
00:18:40,953 --> 00:18:42,830
This situation's already a mess.

283
00:18:43,163 --> 00:18:45,415
Wait. Why are we talking
about him, anyway?

284
00:18:46,333 --> 00:18:50,963
Now that Julio's done for,
Emilia, you should join me.

285
00:18:51,463 --> 00:18:55,259
I'll make you my queen.
You'll be Jaguar Queen.

286
00:18:56,343 --> 00:18:58,762
-Jaguar Queen?
-Yes, Jaguar Queen.

287
00:18:59,888 --> 00:19:02,933
I'll treat you like a queen,
as will my people.

288
00:19:03,350 --> 00:19:05,727
We'll do nothing, Emilia, but get rich.

289
00:19:06,353 --> 00:19:08,647
We're now free to do that
because Julio's over.

290
00:19:08,730 --> 00:19:10,274
No more competition.

291
00:19:10,357 --> 00:19:12,651
[tense music playing]

292
00:19:13,861 --> 00:19:16,613
But, Jaguar, that's not the life I want.

293
00:19:16,697 --> 00:19:18,949
I want to be the queen of Ardiente.

294
00:19:19,032 --> 00:19:21,660
And you will be, Emilia.

295
00:19:22,452 --> 00:19:26,039
As long as our operations are successful.

296
00:19:28,542 --> 00:19:30,919
They'll all bow down
to the queen of Ardiente.

297
00:19:31,003 --> 00:19:32,921
[tense music playing]

298
00:19:40,179 --> 00:19:41,972
I am Lily Cruz.

299
00:19:42,764 --> 00:19:45,517
I pretended to be Ivy Aguas

300
00:19:45,893 --> 00:19:51,106
because I wanted to seek justice
for my family,

301
00:19:51,940 --> 00:19:56,570
and for everyone who was abused
by the Ardientes.

302
00:19:56,945 --> 00:20:00,824
I secretly sabotaged our enemies.

303
00:20:01,491 --> 00:20:06,038
And I secretly helped Diego's camp.

304
00:20:07,206 --> 00:20:11,835
Diego and I, along with my family,

305
00:20:11,919 --> 00:20:15,547
will be the bridges connecting you

306
00:20:15,631 --> 00:20:19,676
to the new government
of Governor Mateo Ruiz.

307
00:20:20,510 --> 00:20:24,223
And I, as one of the owners

308
00:20:24,765 --> 00:20:29,061
of one of the biggest
realty companies in the country,

309
00:20:29,645 --> 00:20:33,982
truly want to help and support you.

310
00:20:34,149 --> 00:20:36,610
[cheers and applause]

311
00:20:36,693 --> 00:20:40,072
[supporters chanting]
Lily Cruz! Lily Cruz!

312
00:20:40,155 --> 00:20:45,160
Lily Cruz! Lily Cruz! Lily Cruz!

313
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:46,578
Please, you don't need to do that.

314
00:20:46,662 --> 00:20:48,914
-I'm not campaigning.
-[chanting continues] Lily Cruz!

315
00:20:48,997 --> 00:20:52,251
-Lily Cruz! Lily Cruz!
-I just want to help.

316
00:20:52,334 --> 00:20:54,294
-Please.
-[chanting continues] Lily Cruz!

317
00:20:54,670 --> 00:20:59,800
Lily Cruz! Lily Cruz! Lily Cruz!

318
00:21:00,676 --> 00:21:01,635
[Lily] Attorney.

319
00:21:02,344 --> 00:21:05,138
Good morning, Lily.
I've taken care of your papers.

320
00:21:05,222 --> 00:21:06,974
You are now back to being Lily Cruz.

321
00:21:07,057 --> 00:21:08,976
[poignant music playing]

322
00:21:09,226 --> 00:21:10,060
Thank you, Attorney.

323
00:21:10,143 --> 00:21:12,938
That includes all
your documents for Aguas Realty.

324
00:21:13,272 --> 00:21:15,482
But I really think
you should go there personally.

325
00:21:15,941 --> 00:21:19,820
All right. I'll see to it.
Please sit down.

326
00:21:25,784 --> 00:21:27,995
It feels so good…

327
00:21:30,956 --> 00:21:32,582
to be Lily Cruz again.

328
00:21:34,418 --> 00:21:39,673
It feels so good because
I no longer have to mingle

329
00:21:39,756 --> 00:21:43,969
with the people I despise,
such as the Ardientes.

330
00:21:44,761 --> 00:21:48,515
I no longer have to keep up pretenses.

331
00:21:48,849 --> 00:21:50,934
Others may think it's as easy

332
00:21:53,228 --> 00:21:55,897
as playing a game.

333
00:21:57,607 --> 00:22:01,486
But it's not. It was never easy.

334
00:22:04,656 --> 00:22:09,494
Ivy Aguas was a very brave woman,

335
00:22:10,537 --> 00:22:16,418
a courageous mask I hid behind
and held on to.

336
00:22:20,464 --> 00:22:21,757
Because I knew

337
00:22:23,925 --> 00:22:26,053
that under the guise of Ivy Aguas,

338
00:22:27,012 --> 00:22:29,765
I could protect myself from the Ardientes.

339
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:34,936
[sighs]

340
00:22:35,020 --> 00:22:39,024
But now that they know the whole truth,

341
00:22:39,941 --> 00:22:46,281
I'm sure they're itching
to exact revenge on me, on you,

342
00:22:47,824 --> 00:22:50,911
and all of my loved ones.

343
00:22:52,579 --> 00:22:55,832
Lily, you'll have to fight them
head-on from now on.

344
00:22:55,916 --> 00:22:57,125
[suspenseful sting]

345
00:22:57,209 --> 00:22:59,127
We know that, and we're ready for it.

346
00:23:00,378 --> 00:23:02,214
At this point, you've already
sacrificed so much

347
00:23:02,297 --> 00:23:03,507
for this fight.

348
00:23:04,424 --> 00:23:06,510
And it's time for you to be happy

349
00:23:07,385 --> 00:23:10,430
by being Lily Cruz, by being true.

350
00:23:10,514 --> 00:23:12,140
I know that's what will make you happy.

351
00:23:13,225 --> 00:23:15,352
You deserve to be happy, dear.

352
00:23:16,603 --> 00:23:17,562
Thank you, Mom.

353
00:23:19,689 --> 00:23:22,067
Anyway, go ahead and eat.
Attorney, please.

354
00:23:23,735 --> 00:23:24,736
Um…

355
00:23:25,946 --> 00:23:28,031
I'll just meet up with Governor Ruiz.

356
00:23:28,115 --> 00:23:31,326
I'm supposed to give him my proposal

357
00:23:31,952 --> 00:23:33,662
regarding Poblacion Ardiente.

358
00:23:35,122 --> 00:23:36,915
-Attorney.
-Take care, dear.

359
00:23:37,165 --> 00:23:38,375
[Lily] I will, Mom.

360
00:23:40,210 --> 00:23:41,795
[spritzing]

361
00:23:43,296 --> 00:23:44,256
[sniffs]

362
00:23:45,173 --> 00:23:48,426
That smells nice. Going out on a date?

363
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:51,221
Um…

364
00:23:51,972 --> 00:23:54,724
Can you please stop
sneaking around like that?

365
00:23:54,808 --> 00:23:56,977
You haven't answered my question.

366
00:23:58,103 --> 00:24:00,772
Okay, Raul. First of all,
I'm not going out on a date.

367
00:24:00,856 --> 00:24:05,110
Second, I don't think
I have to answer your question

368
00:24:05,193 --> 00:24:09,614
because lately, you've had
nothing good to say to Papa.

369
00:24:09,698 --> 00:24:11,950
-So, just keep quiet, okay?
-[scoffs]

370
00:24:12,033 --> 00:24:13,660
You know, I'm honestly surprised

371
00:24:13,910 --> 00:24:15,745
that you're still alive at this point.

372
00:24:15,829 --> 00:24:17,664
That's all because you defended me.

373
00:24:18,123 --> 00:24:20,458
Don't get any ideas, Raul.

374
00:24:20,542 --> 00:24:23,503
Frankly, I pity you. I have to go.

375
00:24:24,171 --> 00:24:26,464
I'm asking you. Who are you meeting?

376
00:24:27,799 --> 00:24:28,967
The governor.

377
00:24:29,301 --> 00:24:31,219
Why? What's your business with him?

378
00:24:32,095 --> 00:24:34,431
Well, you know, Raul,

379
00:24:35,307 --> 00:24:37,434
I was once the queen of Ardiente.

380
00:24:37,517 --> 00:24:39,394
And I am an Ardiente.

381
00:24:39,769 --> 00:24:42,689
So, since Papa has been
unseated as governor,

382
00:24:43,481 --> 00:24:46,484
I'll just prove my worth
that I can still be the queen.

383
00:24:47,569 --> 00:24:49,529
So, if you'll excuse me,

384
00:24:49,988 --> 00:24:51,907
I have to meet with the governor.

385
00:25:05,045 --> 00:25:07,297
[soft piano music playing]

386
00:25:13,970 --> 00:25:14,930
Diego.

387
00:25:15,513 --> 00:25:16,598
Lily.

388
00:25:30,862 --> 00:25:33,114
Ma'am, we'll get going.

389
00:25:33,198 --> 00:25:34,658
You two take care.

390
00:25:38,119 --> 00:25:39,079
Stay safe.

391
00:25:39,162 --> 00:25:40,288
-[Diego] We will.
-[Lily] Bye, Mom.

392
00:25:40,372 --> 00:25:41,164
[Camia] Bye.

393
00:25:41,957 --> 00:25:44,501
[soft piano music playing]

394
00:25:48,129 --> 00:25:49,172
[door closes]

395
00:25:57,013 --> 00:25:58,306
I want you to review all the

396
00:25:58,390 --> 00:26:00,934
-former governor's contracts.
-Ma'am, he's still in a meeting.

397
00:26:01,017 --> 00:26:02,269
[Emilia] Hi, Governor.

398
00:26:05,063 --> 00:26:08,316
Emilia Ardiente-Torillo.
Do we have an appointment?

399
00:26:08,608 --> 00:26:10,151
Now we do, Governor.

400
00:26:10,235 --> 00:26:12,153
Um, gentlemen, will you please excuse me,

401
00:26:12,237 --> 00:26:13,738
so I can fill in the governor?

402
00:26:14,823 --> 00:26:16,074
Gentlemen, can you give us a minute?

403
00:26:16,157 --> 00:26:17,075
-Sure.
-Yes, sir.

404
00:26:19,244 --> 00:26:20,787
-Excuse us.
-Thank you.

405
00:26:21,955 --> 00:26:23,790
Whatever it is, make it quick.

406
00:26:24,082 --> 00:26:25,959
As you can see,
I'm in the middle of a meeting.

407
00:26:31,673 --> 00:26:34,092
So, you like it fast, Governor.

408
00:26:34,676 --> 00:26:36,761
You know, I admire you
for standing your ground

409
00:26:36,845 --> 00:26:38,013
against my papa.

410
00:26:38,555 --> 00:26:43,518
You see, my father still thinks
he is the king of Ardiente,

411
00:26:43,935 --> 00:26:47,314
when in fact, his time is really over.

412
00:26:48,940 --> 00:26:50,483
Can you get to the point?

413
00:26:51,526 --> 00:26:54,029
I want to make a proposal, Governor.

414
00:26:54,904 --> 00:26:55,947
An offer.

415
00:26:58,074 --> 00:27:00,785
I want to be part of your administration.

416
00:27:01,369 --> 00:27:05,040
You see, I'm a former mayor
and governor of this place.

417
00:27:05,957 --> 00:27:08,168
We can help each other a lot.

418
00:27:10,795 --> 00:27:13,798
Governor, I may be an Ardiente,

419
00:27:14,466 --> 00:27:15,800
but the truth is,

420
00:27:16,343 --> 00:27:18,553
we're both victims of my father.

421
00:27:19,346 --> 00:27:23,558
So, if I were to become part of your team,

422
00:27:25,393 --> 00:27:26,519
we'd make magic.

423
00:27:27,562 --> 00:27:29,647
All kinds of magic, Governor.

424
00:27:30,857 --> 00:27:33,485
[suspenseful music playing]

425
00:27:45,872 --> 00:27:47,248
You may leave.

426
00:27:47,540 --> 00:27:49,292
[Emilia breathes deeply]

427
00:27:49,542 --> 00:27:51,753
[suspenseful music playing]

428
00:27:54,214 --> 00:27:55,840
-Governor.
-[Lily clears throat]

429
00:27:59,886 --> 00:28:01,179
Ivy!

430
00:28:02,138 --> 00:28:02,972
It's Lily.

431
00:28:04,933 --> 00:28:07,936
Whatever. Um, Ivy, Lily…

432
00:28:08,019 --> 00:28:10,355
[hissing]

433
00:28:10,688 --> 00:28:14,776
They both sound like
a hissing snake to me.

434
00:28:15,527 --> 00:28:19,030
You know, all this time,
I thought we were friends.

435
00:28:19,447 --> 00:28:23,118
Almost sisters, even.
But little did I know,

436
00:28:23,201 --> 00:28:25,495
you only came here
to take revenge on my family.

437
00:28:25,578 --> 00:28:27,122
You have no right to reproach me,

438
00:28:27,205 --> 00:28:28,706
Emilia Ardiente.

439
00:28:29,040 --> 00:28:32,961
In fact, your soul isn't enough to pay

440
00:28:33,044 --> 00:28:36,005
for all the horrible things
you did to my family!

441
00:28:36,089 --> 00:28:38,550
Why? What are you going to do to me?

442
00:28:39,092 --> 00:28:43,680
Have me killed? Have me raped?
No matter what you want for me,

443
00:28:43,763 --> 00:28:45,390
you can't seem to make it happen.

444
00:28:45,473 --> 00:28:49,519
I mean, look. Look at me now.
I'm still here, aren't I?

445
00:28:49,602 --> 00:28:52,647
And even though we're no longer in power,

446
00:28:52,731 --> 00:28:56,443
I can still make your life miserable.

447
00:28:56,526 --> 00:28:57,777
[suspenseful music playing]

448
00:28:57,861 --> 00:29:00,447
Just accept it, Emilia Ardiente.

449
00:29:00,989 --> 00:29:05,827
Just accept that both you
and your family have lost.

450
00:29:06,077 --> 00:29:11,082
Poblacion Ardiente may be named
after your family,

451
00:29:11,166 --> 00:29:15,670
but let me tell you this.
While I'm still alive, Emilia,

452
00:29:15,754 --> 00:29:20,133
I won't let anyone in your family reign

453
00:29:20,508 --> 00:29:23,428
over Poblacion Ardiente ever again.

454
00:29:23,511 --> 00:29:25,472
[suspenseful music playing]

455
00:29:28,224 --> 00:29:31,978
[Emilia] Diego, get her
iced water so she can chill.

456
00:29:32,312 --> 00:29:34,981
So grumpy today! Huh!

457
00:29:37,901 --> 00:29:40,528
[suspenseful music playing]

458
00:29:46,659 --> 00:29:49,746
I plan to put up a media complex.

459
00:29:50,163 --> 00:29:51,456
Media complex?

460
00:29:52,832 --> 00:29:55,835
Yes. The media complex
will house a tech college,

461
00:29:56,211 --> 00:29:58,588
call center, learning center,

462
00:29:59,214 --> 00:30:02,759
and other venues
for learning and improvement.

463
00:30:03,009 --> 00:30:06,179
And where will you get funding
and sponsors?

464
00:30:06,805 --> 00:30:12,143
Mr. Keng, those two things
won't be problems at all.

465
00:30:12,227 --> 00:30:15,438
I will personally ask certain
parties for their support.

466
00:30:16,105 --> 00:30:18,900
This project will create
opportunities for employment,

467
00:30:18,983 --> 00:30:21,444
and advancement in technology

468
00:30:21,528 --> 00:30:23,404
for the betterment of Poblacion Ardiente.

469
00:30:24,364 --> 00:30:26,282
Your proposal sounds great, Ms. Cruz.

470
00:30:26,950 --> 00:30:28,952
It will surely benefit our province.

471
00:30:29,244 --> 00:30:30,954
Thank you, Governor Ruiz.

472
00:30:31,037 --> 00:30:35,583
And I really count on your full support.

473
00:30:35,667 --> 00:30:37,210
Everyone's support.

474
00:30:46,010 --> 00:30:50,640
So, you're telling me that Ivy
isn't really Ivy Aguas?

475
00:30:51,641 --> 00:30:55,937
You're telling me that she is Lily Cruz?

476
00:30:56,020 --> 00:30:57,105
Yes, ma'am.

477
00:30:57,647 --> 00:30:58,898
That's crazy.

478
00:30:59,440 --> 00:31:04,529
For someone who brought down
the whole Ardiente empire,

479
00:31:05,196 --> 00:31:08,032
she's named Lily Cruz?

480
00:31:08,116 --> 00:31:08,950
[laughs]

481
00:31:09,492 --> 00:31:11,369
That's such a weak name!

482
00:31:12,161 --> 00:31:13,204
[chuckles]

483
00:31:13,705 --> 00:31:15,748
She sounds way too innocent.

484
00:31:15,832 --> 00:31:16,791
[inhales sharply]

485
00:31:17,917 --> 00:31:20,128
Is she the one you were helping?

486
00:31:20,503 --> 00:31:22,422
Is that why you were always away?

487
00:31:24,090 --> 00:31:27,302
Ma'am, you know I can't just leave them.

488
00:31:27,802 --> 00:31:29,929
Why do you waste so much time with them?

489
00:31:32,765 --> 00:31:36,978
Well, now that the Ardientes
have lost their power,

490
00:31:37,353 --> 00:31:41,608
now is the perfect time
for us to put up our own empire.

491
00:31:42,483 --> 00:31:44,652
You and me.

492
00:31:45,612 --> 00:31:46,654
[foreboding music playing]

493
00:31:46,738 --> 00:31:50,950
I can be queen, and maybe…

494
00:31:51,826 --> 00:31:54,120
you could be king.

495
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:56,122
Ma'am, don't.

496
00:31:59,167 --> 00:32:00,668
You know it's pointless.

497
00:32:01,544 --> 00:32:04,088
I don't want to join any gang

498
00:32:04,714 --> 00:32:05,924
or take part in any of your plans.

499
00:32:06,841 --> 00:32:09,010
Stop bugging me. I don't need you.

500
00:32:17,977 --> 00:32:24,692
Are you sure you don't need me?
So, why are you here?

501
00:32:28,029 --> 00:32:29,739
Did they reject you?

502
00:32:32,659 --> 00:32:34,619
Did they make you jealous?

503
00:32:36,704 --> 00:32:40,667
Or… you just want to de-stress?

504
00:32:42,919 --> 00:32:46,547
Whatever your reason is, I don't care.

505
00:32:47,131 --> 00:32:49,300
What's important to me

506
00:32:50,009 --> 00:32:53,137
is that brought you here.

507
00:32:55,181 --> 00:32:58,685
That's why I'll never let you go.

508
00:32:59,978 --> 00:33:01,521
Never again.

509
00:33:01,980 --> 00:33:04,482
[dark sensual music playing]

510
00:33:10,780 --> 00:33:11,614
Ma'am.

511
00:33:11,698 --> 00:33:13,241
[breathes deeply]

512
00:33:13,324 --> 00:33:14,450
Ma'am, hold on.

513
00:33:15,994 --> 00:33:16,869
Ma'am!

514
00:33:27,839 --> 00:33:29,132
[Jepoy exhales sharply]

515
00:33:29,215 --> 00:33:31,134
[footsteps departing]

516
00:33:35,972 --> 00:33:38,141
You can throw a tantrum
all you want, Governor.

517
00:33:39,017 --> 00:33:40,226
But that's not going to help.

518
00:33:40,977 --> 00:33:44,105
And what do you expect me to do?!

519
00:33:45,690 --> 00:33:47,483
I advise you to wait it out.

520
00:33:48,484 --> 00:33:50,611
Take a break. Lie low.

521
00:33:51,779 --> 00:33:53,656
This is not your arena anymore, Governor.

522
00:33:53,906 --> 00:33:56,200
Mateo Ruiz is officially the governor now.

523
00:33:56,659 --> 00:33:58,786
Don't lose yourself
in fighting a lost game,

524
00:33:59,245 --> 00:34:02,915
or else, it'll be harder for you
to restore your reputation.

525
00:34:05,501 --> 00:34:06,502
Darn it.

526
00:34:06,586 --> 00:34:07,670
Excuse me, Governor.

527
00:34:08,171 --> 00:34:10,590
Go ahead. Leave.

528
00:34:15,636 --> 00:34:17,764
Papa, I see you're upset again.

529
00:34:18,306 --> 00:34:22,351
I thought you had a meeting
with Mateo Ruiz.

530
00:34:22,560 --> 00:34:25,938
Yes, I did, Papa.
But he refused my proposal.

531
00:34:26,814 --> 00:34:29,609
That cave-dwelling troglodyte!

532
00:34:29,692 --> 00:34:30,735
[suspenseful sting]

533
00:34:31,402 --> 00:34:33,154
Who does he think he is?

534
00:34:34,238 --> 00:34:38,826
You know, Emilia,
for the first time in history,

535
00:34:39,535 --> 00:34:42,455
this province isn't governed
by an Ardiente.

536
00:34:42,955 --> 00:34:44,373
I cannot take this!

537
00:34:45,083 --> 00:34:47,627
You have to help me.
This can't be happening.

538
00:34:49,545 --> 00:34:53,382
Why, Papa? Did you ever help me?

539
00:34:55,760 --> 00:34:57,345
I had your case dismissed!

540
00:34:57,428 --> 00:34:58,888
Come on, Papa!

541
00:34:58,971 --> 00:35:03,017
I know the truth already.
It wasn't you who helped me out!

542
00:35:03,101 --> 00:35:06,145
You know, the only reason
I am here in this house

543
00:35:06,229 --> 00:35:09,440
is that I want to know
who my real mother is!

544
00:35:09,524 --> 00:35:11,067
That's the truth, Papa!

545
00:35:11,484 --> 00:35:14,821
Because only my mother can help me.

546
00:35:14,904 --> 00:35:16,364
She alone and not you!

547
00:35:16,447 --> 00:35:19,367
[dramatic tense music playing]

548
00:35:19,450 --> 00:35:20,451
[exhales sharply]

549
00:35:22,912 --> 00:35:23,788
[thuds]

550
00:35:24,163 --> 00:35:28,918
I am Julio Ardiente! I am not nothing!

551
00:35:29,252 --> 00:35:31,879
[breathing heavily]

552
00:35:36,134 --> 00:35:38,136
As you all know, I was adopted.

553
00:35:39,679 --> 00:35:43,516
But now, Ivy Aguas is dead.

554
00:35:45,393 --> 00:35:49,981
From this day forward,
you will address me by my real name.

555
00:35:52,567 --> 00:35:53,943
Lily Cruz.

556
00:35:54,026 --> 00:35:55,820
[murmuring]

557
00:35:56,320 --> 00:35:57,947
Is that understood?

558
00:35:58,030 --> 00:35:59,240
-Yes, ma'am.
-Yes.

559
00:36:00,491 --> 00:36:02,702
Have you finished your project
in Ardiente?

560
00:36:03,327 --> 00:36:06,497
I'm starting another one.
What's next on the agenda?

561
00:36:09,542 --> 00:36:11,794
Ms. Cruz, we need to set
a meeting with you

562
00:36:11,878 --> 00:36:13,462
and Mrs. Helena Montoya.

563
00:36:16,966 --> 00:36:18,509
Who's Helena Montoya?

564
00:36:18,593 --> 00:36:20,720
She's the CEO of Montoya Industries,

565
00:36:20,803 --> 00:36:23,514
and she's interested in investing

566
00:36:23,598 --> 00:36:27,185
in our luxury residences project
in the suburbs.

567
00:36:27,268 --> 00:36:28,769
She made a great offer.

568
00:36:32,106 --> 00:36:33,733
Montoya Industries?

569
00:36:35,568 --> 00:36:36,777
Never heard of it.

570
00:36:41,365 --> 00:36:44,452
Don't set a meeting with Helena Montoya.

571
00:36:44,535 --> 00:36:45,661
Not yet.

572
00:36:45,745 --> 00:36:49,457
Instead, I want you
to research her company.

573
00:36:50,750 --> 00:36:51,667
And you?

574
00:36:52,376 --> 00:36:56,172
Do a background check
on this Helena Montoya.

575
00:36:56,756 --> 00:36:58,049
Certainly, Ms. Cruz.

576
00:37:13,898 --> 00:37:16,275
[opens, then closes drawer]

577
00:37:16,943 --> 00:37:19,237
[unsettling music playing]

578
00:37:21,489 --> 00:37:23,991
[line ringing]

579
00:37:24,992 --> 00:37:26,202
Hello, Romulo.

580
00:37:26,452 --> 00:37:27,787
I know you are there.

581
00:37:28,412 --> 00:37:30,915
Come on, please.
I just want to know the truth.

582
00:37:31,165 --> 00:37:36,045
Who told you to help me? Hello? Hello?!

583
00:37:40,424 --> 00:37:41,968
-[line beeping]
-[exhales sharply]

584
00:37:51,352 --> 00:37:52,520
[line ringing]

585
00:37:52,895 --> 00:37:53,938
Hello, Attorney.

586
00:37:54,272 --> 00:37:55,564
Can you tell me again the address

587
00:37:55,648 --> 00:37:57,024
I asked you to research?

588
00:37:57,566 --> 00:38:00,069
The one owned by Mercedes Palacio.

589
00:38:04,949 --> 00:38:06,826
[tense music playing]

590
00:38:13,499 --> 00:38:15,293
[Emilia] <i>Who ordered you</i>
<i>to kidnap me? Huh?!</i>

591
00:38:15,376 --> 00:38:17,044
<i>Who?! Answer me!</i>

592
00:38:17,295 --> 00:38:19,046
[Robert] <i>I tracked down</i>
<i>the owner of the house</i>

593
00:38:19,130 --> 00:38:20,298
<i>where those men brought you.</i>

594
00:38:20,381 --> 00:38:23,134
<i>They're both registered</i>
<i>to one Mercedes Palacio.</i>

595
00:38:23,217 --> 00:38:24,468
<i>Huh? Who is she?</i>

596
00:38:30,391 --> 00:38:31,225
[man] Ma'am.

597
00:38:32,351 --> 00:38:34,061
Is Mercedes Palacio around?

598
00:38:34,145 --> 00:38:36,147
Ma'am, I was told she rarely comes here.

599
00:38:36,230 --> 00:38:39,066
[suspenseful music playing]

600
00:38:51,662 --> 00:38:52,663
[car door closes]

601
00:38:58,252 --> 00:38:59,962
[suspenseful music playing]

602
00:39:04,592 --> 00:39:05,718
Looking for me?

603
00:39:07,928 --> 00:39:09,263
Mercedes Palacio?

604
00:39:09,972 --> 00:39:12,475
Absolutely. Who else?

605
00:39:15,144 --> 00:39:17,480
[suspenseful music intensifies]

606
00:39:23,277 --> 00:39:25,446
My father keeps blaming me, when in fact,

607
00:39:25,529 --> 00:39:27,782
he didn't lift a finger to help me.

608
00:39:28,741 --> 00:39:32,244
Didn't you and Romulo save my life?

609
00:39:32,661 --> 00:39:36,540
Why did you save me?
Is it because of my real mom?

610
00:39:37,124 --> 00:39:39,752
Do you work for her? Is she your boss?

611
00:39:40,211 --> 00:39:42,922
One at a time. You ask too many questions.

612
00:39:43,589 --> 00:39:47,093
What's more important to you?
Becoming the queen of Ardiente,

613
00:39:47,176 --> 00:39:49,512
or discovering your mom's identity?

614
00:39:50,346 --> 00:39:52,431
[tense music playing]

615
00:39:54,350 --> 00:39:55,434
Both.

616
00:39:56,936 --> 00:39:58,938
I want to be the queen of Ardiente,

617
00:39:59,814 --> 00:40:06,737
and have acting governor
Mateo Ruiz at my beck and call.

618
00:40:09,240 --> 00:40:10,366
Are you up for it?

619
00:40:13,411 --> 00:40:14,703
Is that all?

620
00:40:16,497 --> 00:40:19,291
[suspenseful music playing]

621
00:40:29,927 --> 00:40:30,970
Who are they?

622
00:40:42,857 --> 00:40:43,816
[bodyguard grunts]

623
00:40:45,401 --> 00:40:48,446
[screaming, grunting]

624
00:40:53,742 --> 00:40:54,785
[thuds]

625
00:40:55,411 --> 00:40:57,246
[suspenseful music playing]

626
00:41:10,217 --> 00:41:11,260
Who are you?

627
00:41:11,594 --> 00:41:14,889
Don't worry. We won't hurt you.

628
00:41:15,181 --> 00:41:17,308
Do you work for Julio Ardiente?

629
00:41:17,391 --> 00:41:18,309
[scoffs]

630
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:22,646
What do you want from me?

631
00:41:23,272 --> 00:41:24,982
Someone wants to see you.

632
00:41:25,733 --> 00:41:26,734
Who?

633
00:41:29,111 --> 00:41:30,571
Red Dragon.

634
00:41:45,920 --> 00:41:49,340
I'm sure the governor will love your plan.

635
00:41:51,008 --> 00:41:52,301
Thanks, Diego.

636
00:41:55,262 --> 00:41:56,263
[Mateo clears throat]

637
00:41:56,972 --> 00:41:57,890
Governor.

638
00:41:58,432 --> 00:41:59,350
Good afternoon.

639
00:41:59,892 --> 00:42:00,935
Governor.

640
00:42:08,567 --> 00:42:11,487
Okay, shall we start?
Good morning, everyone.

641
00:42:11,570 --> 00:42:12,530
-Today--
-[Mateo] Wait.

642
00:42:13,948 --> 00:42:15,241
We can't start just yet.

643
00:42:16,242 --> 00:42:18,702
Why, Governor? Looks like everyone's here.

644
00:42:19,370 --> 00:42:20,204
We're still waiting for someone.

645
00:42:20,287 --> 00:42:22,248
[tense music playing]

646
00:42:22,748 --> 00:42:24,542
-Who?
-Me.

647
00:42:27,253 --> 00:42:29,129
I'm so sorry I'm late.

648
00:42:35,261 --> 00:42:37,054
Governor, is this a joke?!

649
00:42:37,721 --> 00:42:43,561
Governor, I thought Lily Cruz
was aware that I'd be here

650
00:42:43,644 --> 00:42:47,481
to give my opinion on her
little project for Ardiente.

651
00:42:47,565 --> 00:42:51,610
After all, that's what
a consultant does, right?

652
00:42:52,861 --> 00:42:54,863
Yes, you heard it right.

653
00:42:55,322 --> 00:42:59,118
I am now the consultant
of Governor Mateo Ruiz.

654
00:42:59,201 --> 00:43:02,705
I will help him with decisions
concerning this province.

655
00:43:02,788 --> 00:43:04,790
What is this, Governor?
Are you kidding me?

656
00:43:05,833 --> 00:43:07,585
Are you kidding me?!

657
00:43:07,668 --> 00:43:08,877
Ms. Cruz,

658
00:43:09,211 --> 00:43:12,423
why are you so surprised that
he got me as his consultant?

659
00:43:12,506 --> 00:43:13,716
Have you forgotten?

660
00:43:13,882 --> 00:43:16,552
I used to be the mayor
and the governor of this--

661
00:43:16,635 --> 00:43:18,053
Yeah, right!

662
00:43:18,137 --> 00:43:19,888
-Mayor Corrupt Queen,
-[suspenseful music playing]

663
00:43:19,972 --> 00:43:23,934
and Governor Murderer
of Poblacion Ardiente!

664
00:43:24,018 --> 00:43:25,769
Ms. Cruz, calm yourself!

665
00:43:27,605 --> 00:43:29,607
Our province is already divided,

666
00:43:29,898 --> 00:43:32,610
and this is the first step to peace.

667
00:43:32,693 --> 00:43:35,195
For us to come and work together

668
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:36,572
for the progress of our province.

669
00:43:36,655 --> 00:43:39,491
Exactly! We're divided
and we need to help one another

670
00:43:39,575 --> 00:43:41,243
but what are you doing, Governor?!

671
00:43:41,327 --> 00:43:42,494
What happened to you?!

672
00:43:43,245 --> 00:43:46,248
Did these criminals threaten you?! Huh?!

673
00:43:47,958 --> 00:43:50,044
Tell me, what did they do to you?

674
00:43:50,127 --> 00:43:52,713
Did they hurt your family?
Is Julio behind this?

675
00:43:52,796 --> 00:43:53,922
-What? Tell me--
-No!

676
00:43:54,673 --> 00:43:57,885
I made this decision for
the betterment of our province!

677
00:43:59,136 --> 00:44:00,596
We don't believe you.

678
00:44:01,221 --> 00:44:03,182
Governor, you know the Ardientes.

679
00:44:03,265 --> 00:44:04,933
You know they aren't capable of good.

680
00:44:05,643 --> 00:44:08,437
You betrayed your promise to the people.

681
00:44:08,937 --> 00:44:10,147
You made fools of us.

682
00:44:11,607 --> 00:44:18,572
Governor Ruiz, we had
an agreement, remember?

683
00:44:18,947 --> 00:44:24,953
We promised to help each other.
So, please. I'm telling you.

684
00:44:25,037 --> 00:44:28,999
You don't have to be afraid
of the Ardientes!

685
00:44:29,083 --> 00:44:32,920
Enough of this drama, Ms. Cruz.
Whether you like it or not,

686
00:44:33,003 --> 00:44:35,964
I am now the consultant
of Governor Mateo Ruiz.

687
00:44:36,632 --> 00:44:39,635
Meanwhile, you're just another nuisance

688
00:44:39,718 --> 00:44:42,846
who wants a taste
of the governor's graces.

689
00:44:43,430 --> 00:44:45,891
Well, I'm happy to say this.

690
00:44:45,974 --> 00:44:47,643
I am here to protect the governor

691
00:44:47,726 --> 00:44:49,186
from leeches like you!

692
00:44:49,269 --> 00:44:51,605
You're the leech in this town!

693
00:44:52,064 --> 00:44:55,275
You're sucking
Poblacion Ardiente's wealth!

694
00:44:55,359 --> 00:44:56,819
You are the leech!

695
00:44:56,902 --> 00:44:59,988
Well, guess what.
Whether you like it or not,

696
00:45:00,280 --> 00:45:02,241
I get to decide for the governor.

697
00:45:03,575 --> 00:45:06,495
And if I were you,
I'd be on my best behavior.

698
00:45:07,329 --> 00:45:10,499
If you want to be in or out.

699
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:14,169
Not here.

700
00:45:14,253 --> 00:45:15,754
[chuckles] Mm-mm.

701
00:45:17,965 --> 00:45:21,176
[dramatic tense music playing]

702
00:45:33,689 --> 00:45:37,693
[gloomy music playing]

703
00:45:44,324 --> 00:45:47,244
[gloomy tense music playing]

704
00:46:04,803 --> 00:46:08,807
Madam, here's the research you ordered.

705
00:46:09,975 --> 00:46:13,645
[suspenseful music playing]

706
00:46:28,452 --> 00:46:31,205
[suspenseful music playing]

707
00:46:47,304 --> 00:46:48,764
<i>Ma'am, sir! It's Sir Arnaldo.</i>

708
00:46:48,847 --> 00:46:50,349
<i>Why? What happened to my grandson?</i>

709
00:46:50,891 --> 00:46:51,892
<i>Arnaldo?</i>

710
00:46:52,309 --> 00:46:53,477
<i>-Arnaldo.</i>
-[Emilia] <i>Arnaldo.</i>

711
00:46:53,560 --> 00:46:54,603
<i>Who are you?</i>

712
00:46:57,523 --> 00:47:01,902
<i>We won't lose to the Ardientes.</i>
<i>We can take them on!</i>

713
00:47:01,985 --> 00:47:04,780
<i>It's about time we let her know</i>

714
00:47:04,863 --> 00:47:06,907
<i>that you're not to be messed with.</i>

715
00:47:06,990 --> 00:47:08,283
[beeping]

716
00:47:10,160 --> 00:47:12,496
[Lily] <i>At this point,</i>
<i>we shouldn't trust anyone.</i>

717
00:47:12,579 --> 00:47:15,332
<i>We don't know who we're up against.</i>

718
00:47:17,501 --> 00:47:20,003
[beeping]

719
00:47:20,087 --> 00:47:22,673
[theme music playing]
